  "local_summary": "This document chronicles a multi-cycle research task aimed at retrieving detailed descriptions and track chair profiles for specific tracks (3, 4, 5, 7) of the POM Fukuoka 2027 conference. The core conceptual move is the progressive encounter with, and theoretical re-framing of, infrastructural gatekeeping mechanisms (e.g., Cloudflare CAPTCHA) as active material boundaries rather than mere technical failures. Initial attempts at direct extraction are met with anti-bot measures, leading to fragmented insights. The task confirms the overarching conference theme ('Culturing Transduction') and the participation of M. Beatrice Fazi as co-chair for Track 3, along with details for Track 1. \n\nTensions arise between the stated objective of comprehensive information retrieval and the reality of algorithmic exclusion, leading to an epistemic pivot where technical obstacles are interpreted through theoretical lenses (new materialism, anti-interactionism) as significant data points about academic enclosures and apparatuses. The document explicitly critiques its own 'institutional extraction bias' and 'anglophone academic indexation bias.' \n\nThe primary unresolved thread is the lack of complete, verified details for Tracks 3 (full co-chairs), 4, 5, and 7, leading to a decision to continue the research. The process highlights the challenge of navigating distributed information across fragmented digital landscapes and the 'material voice' of computational infrastructure.\n\n\n",
